              <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4">
                <p class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Prevention tips</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">Arrive gradually if possible (spend a night at 2,400m Lijiang first). Drink 3-4 liters of water daily. Avoid alcohol for the first 48 hours. Eat light, high-carb meals.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4">
                <p class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Medication</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">Diamox (acetazolamide) 125mg twice daily starting 1-2 days before arrival significantly reduces symptoms. Oxygen canisters (30-50 RMB) available everywhere. Ibuprofen helps with headaches.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4">
                <p class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">When to descend</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">If you experience severe headache unresponsive to medication, confusion, difficulty breathing at rest, or chest tightness, descend immediately. Diqing has a hospital with altitude sickness expertise.</p>
